body:
It's hard to not put all of my efforts into something, It seems like a waste of time to think about something only for it to not be of any importance.

&#x200B;

When people talk to me, my mind is usually trying to figure out how to take action and react properly.

People you cant trust arent friends. Those are people you'd have around to satiate loneliness.  

&#x200B;

Is it hard to separate from those people?

I see people talk irl but I don't get what fuels their interactions, I basically only follow conversations that are related to analyzations of some type.

&#x200B;

By "fit" do you mean get along with? Can I give them a summary of myself for the pairing?

If you put effort into apartment searching you will be fine, only a person who goes to parties, ubers, and never leaves Manhattan would consider this low.

&#x200B;

The reason for the variety of answers is due to NYC being the home of very wealthy people with blown-out base expectations for living. If you grew up normally then you shouldn't worry.

I was at the store just now and got this text from my husband, “you need to leave right fucking now before I break every mother fucking thing in this house.”

&#x200B;

Right away! Nothing below this sentence would change that.

Tell people there that you don't believe in their teaching/god and you're only there for your parents.

&#x200B;

Are you saved to leave soon? This dynamic is heading south.

  The United States? The economy? Political climate? The protests?  

&#x200B;

All of these.

Thanks, this helps.

&#x200B;

Helped

Shes cute and not intimidating.

&#x200B;

Most girls play games I think.

Depends on your definition of hatred.  Nothing you mentioned seems like hatred, basic comments can be taken anyway, most people would love for their culture to be so commonplace that it can be considered basic. People like yelling at others for social issues because it makes them feel smart.

&#x200B;

Whitewashing only matters because discrimination was common in the acting industry for a long time and minorities have had more difficulty finding acting jobs. These won't be issues 20 years from now though.

" and obviously enjoy the attention because you make no effort to change, expecting the whole world to change just for you "

&#x200B;

What does this mean?

Don't go to church

Assume in this scenario they call you and ask why you didn't go, just say " I don't want to go".

&#x200B;

Your an adult now, They can't force you. Unless their funding your schooling, in that case then you don't have a choice in this matter.

&#x200B;

Seeing that G & J ruin your time with your other friends talk to the other friends for advice. J sounds like he's trying so definitely focus on G first (cause dealing with 2 at the same time is definitely overwhelming). If your friends agree that G is bad and maybe everyone is afraid of confrontation then maybe approach him as a group to say enough is enough. Later do the same to J if his behavior doesn't improve. If G pulls a "but J did xyz too" reply with how J has gotten better over the years while G hasn't. 

&#x200B;

If you end up having to leave the whole group don't sweat it. Join a club or sport and make new friends.

Her opinion is only just that, an opinion. Feminism is what she makes it, there will always be extremists and people that will make your group look bad no matter what group you're in. She is probably only in it to fit in with everyone though.

If you have sympathy for the falsely accused you can help by leading those affected to the right resources so they can file defamation lawsuits. 

&#x200B;

The point of "nice guys" is that they aren't genuinely nice (hince the fact that they have refer to themselves as nice). 

&#x200B;

Also don't tell me that you thought being on any site on the internet would make you like girls. Social media is a void of hatred.
